  "id": "epilepsy-surgery",
  "term": "epilepsy surgery",
  "definition": "Epilepsy surgery is an operation used to reduce seizures in people with epilepsy, especially temporal lobe epilepsy, though some patients still continue to have seizures afterward. In this assessment context, the term also refers to evaluating likely surgical outcome using clinical, pathological, and neuropsychological information before the procedure.",
